[00:00.0 --> 00:05.0]
rysh-server: the hub that routes shares between machines.

[00:05.0 --> 00:15.0]
rysh-server is the optional upstream hub. Local sessions connect to it to share panes, groups, and tabs with collaborators on other machines.

[00:15.0 --> 00:26.0]
Under the hood it is Go and Gin for the API, PostgreSQL for persistence, an embedded NATS server for real-time messaging, and nginx out front.

[00:26.0 --> 00:37.0]
The server handles authentication with JWT or Firebase, and it owns workspaces, members, API keys, and the routing and access control for every share.

[00:37.0 --> 00:50.0]
It ships as a Docker Compose stack -- make dev-up for development, make prod-up for production -- so you can stand up your own hub in minutes.

